The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> has an IP68 dust and water resistance rating, beating Samsung and tying Google.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-hero.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063424" /><br/>
Samsung's latest Galaxy Z Fold8 models have an IP48 dust and water resistance rating, which means they aren't able to hold up to dust as well. Google's Pixel 11 Pro Fold also has an IP68 rating.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://iec.ch/ip-ratings">IP6X for dust</a> means the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is "dust-tight" and no dust is able to get in. The IPX8 rating for water means it is protected from water deeper than 1 meter. Apple says the device can handle a maximum depth of 6 meters for up to 30 minutes. IP68 is the same dust and water resistance rating as other iPhones, and dust matters because it can <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/13/ifixit-galaxy-z-fold8-teardown/">get into the hinges</a> of foldables and cause damage.<br/>
<br/>
